# The trailing whitespace in this file is the test fixture, not an accident.
# tests/parity/gsea/corpus.py writes it on purpose so that the
# `gmt_trailing_whitespace` case can record what mageckGSEA does with a GMT
# line that ends in spaces: `while(ss.good())` runs one iteration past the
# last token and a phantom empty gene name joins the set, inflating the Size
# column. Stripping it would delete the case. Exempt it from the whitespace
# checks so `git diff --check` stays useful everywhere else.
tests/parity/gsea/goldens/gmt_trailing_whitespace/sets.gmt -whitespace
